<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78196" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά-κλητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>called to one's aid</i>,
			in a court of justice : as Subst., <i>legal assistant,
				advocate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lycurg.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				102
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>summoned</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					46.20
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				601.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>intercessor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.520
			</span></i> : hence in <u>NT</u>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παράκλητος</span>, of the Holy Spirit, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
				14.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Jo.</u>
				2.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
